{
  "//": [
    "Copy to .claude/settings.local.json for personal, uncommitted overrides.",
    "This file is an example and is NOT read by Claude Code.",
    "Local settings sit above the shared project file, below managed settings."
  ],

  "//model": "Pin a model for this repo only, without changing your global default.",
  "model": "claude-opus-5-5",

  "//permissions": [
    "Two opposite postures you might want locally.",
    "",
    "A) Tighter than the team file — forbid the escape hatches entirely:",
    "     \"disableBypassPermissionsMode\": \"disable\"  blocks --dangerously-skip-permissions",
    "     \"disableAutoMode\": \"disable\"               blocks --permission-mode auto",
    "   Neither can be re-enabled by a flag once set, which is the point.",
    "",
    "B) Looser — stop being asked about the things you always say yes to.",
    "   Allow rules in a LOCAL file apply without the workspace-trust step, which is why",
    "   'Yes, and don't ask again' writes here rather than into the shared file."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "disableBypassPermissionsMode": "disable",
    "allow": [
      "Bash(./gradlew *)",
      "Bash(xcodebuild *)",
      "Bash(adb *)"
    ],
    "additionalDirectories": [
      "../streakkit-design-notes"
    ]
  },

  "//enabledMcpjsonServers": [
    "The shared file enables only the local 'streakkit' server, because the others need",
    "credentials or a network. Opt into the rest here once you have set the tokens.",
    "github needs GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN exported in your shell."
  ],
  "enabledMcpjsonServers": ["streakkit", "github", "filesystem", "context7"],

  "//autoCompactThreshold": "Compact earlier than the default on a repo with long Gradle output.",
  "autoCompactThreshold": 0.7
}
